    "notes": [
      {
        "id": "note-about",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 256,
        "h": 624,
        "color": "blue",
        "text": "---\nlabel: About\n---\n# Health access in Rwanda\n\nHow many people live more than 5 km from a public health facility, district by district? Five kilometres is about an hour's walk."
      },
      {
        "id": "note-data",
        "x": 280,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 240,
        "h": 624,
        "color": "green",
        "text": "---\nlabel: Input data\n---\n## Three open datasets\n\nPeople per hexagon, public health facilities and district boundaries."
      },
      {
        "id": "note-distance",
        "x": 544,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 544,
        "h": 624,
        "color": "yellow",
        "text": "---\nlabel: Step 1\n---\n## Distance to the nearest facility\n\nThe middle of each hexagon finds its nearest facility in a straight line, and the people more than 5 km away are kept. Roads and hills make the real journey longer."
      },
      {
        "id": "note-districts",
        "x": 1112,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 368,
        "h": 624,
        "color": "yellow",
        "text": "---\nlabel: Step 2\n---\n## People per district\n\nTwo spatial joins add up each district's people: everyone, and those more than 5 km away."
      },
      {
        "id": "note-share",
        "x": 1504,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 240,
        "h": 624,
        "color": "yellow",
        "text": "---\nlabel: Result\n---\n## Share per district\n\nEach district's share of people more than 5 km from a facility."
      }
